{"name":"India Trade","hex":"#e0a362","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"india","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of India of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of India from the NATO/ICAO Phonetic Alphabet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/india"},{"term":"trade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The buying and selling of goods and services on a market.","A particular instance of buying or selling, or a series of related transactions executed as a single investment."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To engage in trade. .mw-parser-output .object-usage-tag{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output .deprecated{color:var(--wikt-palette-grey-lime-8,olivedrab)}[transitive or with in ‘something’, along with with ‘somebody’]","To be traded at a certain price or under certain conditions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trade"}],"entries":[{"title":"India","blocks":[{"text":"India, officially the Republic of India, is a country in South Asia. It is the world's seventh-largest country by area and its most populous. Bounded by the Indian Ocean on the south, the Arabian Sea on the southwest, and the Bay of Bengal on the southeast, it shares land borders with Pakistan to the west, China, Nepal, and Bhutan to the north, and Bangladesh and Myanmar to the east. In the Indian Ocean, India is near Sri Lanka and the Maldives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/41/Flag_of_India.svg/330px-Flag_of_India.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India","wikidata":"Q668"},{"title":"Trade","blocks":[{"text":"Trade is the act by which people swap something of value to obtain another valuable item. It involves the transfer of goods and services from one person or entity (seller) to another (buyer), often in exchange for money.